  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "Given:\n\n(9, 26, 53)\n\n(8, 23, 47)\n\n**Logic: Third **number** = [(First **number** × 3) + Second **number**]**\n\n**(9, 26, 53) →**\n\n⇒ [(9 × 3) + 26]\n\n⇒ (27 + 26) = 53\n\n**(8, 23, 47) →**\n\n⇒ [(8 × 3) + 23]\n\n⇒ (24 + 23) = 47\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. (5, 14, 29)**\n\n⇒ [(5 × 3) + 14]\n\n⇒ (15 + 14) =** 29 = Third number**\n\n2. (6, 17, 36)\n\n⇒ [(6 × 3) + 17]\n\n⇒ (18 + 17) = 35\n\n3. (11, 32, 56)\n\n⇒ [(11 × 3) + 32]\n\n⇒ (33 + 32) = 65\n\n4. (7, 20, 42)\n\n⇒ [(7 × 3) + 20]\n\n⇒ (21 + 22) = 41\n\nHere, **(5, 14, 29)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (1)\".",
